riscv64 zkVM: memmove past the inline threshold is the ZisK DMA idiom, not three frames

A DMA-backed copy cost about 35 executed instructions of overhead regardless of size:
SpanHelpers.Memmove's frame and checks (20), the MemmoveNative shim with its frame, the two
pinning stores and their clears (13), and the libziskos wrapper (csrs; add x0; ret). The traced
Nethermind block made 47k such copies.

JIT: JitZkCsrPInvokes entries with three arguments are emitted in the DMA shape libziskos uses,
`csrrs x0, csr, a1` (source) followed by `add x0, a0, a2` (destination, length), with no call and
no register kills, like the one-argument precompile form of perf-56. bflat adds
memmove:813,memcpy:813 for the zisk libc.

CoreLib (riscv64 only): MemmoveNative passes the refs as pointers - the uGC never moves objects,
so pinning is redundant - and is AggressiveInlining, so Memmove's native path becomes the two
DMA instructions in line and Memmove itself has no call left to save RA for.

diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp b/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp
index 2678154aa..24ef90ce4 100644
--- a/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp
@@ -6029,6 +6029,18 @@ void CodeGen::genCallInstruction(GenTreeCall* call)
     const int zkCsr = m_compiler->zkCsrForPInvoke(call);
     if (zkCsr >= 0)
     {
+        if (call->gtArgs.CountArgs() == 3)
+        {
+            // ZisK DMA copy, as libziskos' memmove/memcpy wrappers spell it: the CSR takes the source
+            // and the following `add x0, dst, len` carries the other two operands.
+            const ABIPassingSegment& dst = call->gtArgs.GetArgByIndex(0)->AbiInfo.Segment(0);
+            const ABIPassingSegment& src = call->gtArgs.GetArgByIndex(1)->AbiInfo.Segment(0);
+            const ABIPassingSegment& len = call->gtArgs.GetArgByIndex(2)->AbiInfo.Segment(0);
+            assert(dst.IsPassedInRegister() && src.IsPassedInRegister() && len.IsPassedInRegister());
+            GetEmitter()->emitIns_R_R_I(INS_csrrs, EA_8BYTE, REG_ZERO, src.GetRegister(), zkCsr);
+            GetEmitter()->emitIns_R_R_R(INS_add, EA_8BYTE, REG_ZERO, dst.GetRegister(), len.GetRegister());
+            return;
+        }
         const ABIPassingSegment& seg = call->gtArgs.GetArgByIndex(0)->AbiInfo.Segment(0);
         assert(seg.IsPassedInRegister());
         GetEmitter()->emitIns_R_R_I(INS_csrrs, EA_8BYTE, REG_ZERO, seg.GetRegister(), zkCsr);
diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/jitconfigvalues.h b/src/coreclr/jit/jitconfigvalues.h
